<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.9.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02486</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.9.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ff943303-0f72-4033-9932-710247c39ba6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice">
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
        <exercise id="_73e4ba8b-5ba4-41b1-8314-aae3db1bcec7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following points is the vertex of the quadratic function \(f(x)=x^2+8x+22\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((8, 22)\)</para>
            <para>\((0, 22)\)</para>
            <para>\((-4, 6)\)</para>
            <para>\((4, 6)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((-4, 6)\)</para>
            <para>\((\frac{b}{2})^2=(\frac{8}{2})^2=16\) \(f(x)=x^2+8x+16+22-16\) \(f(x)=x^2+8x+16+22-16\) \(f(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) \(f(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) Vertex: \((-4, 6)\) Vertex: \((-4, 6)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \((-4, 6)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8585ee96-150f-4228-848f-ad2e0dccfa9c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 2 – 4, use the function \(f(x)=(x-4)(x+2)\).</para>
            <para>Write the function in standard form.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=x^2-2x-8\)</para>
            <para>Expand: \(f(x)=(x-4)(x+2)\) \(f(x)=(x-4)(x+2)\) \(f(x)=x^2-4x+2x-8\) \(f(x)=x^2-4x+2x-8\) \(f(x)=x^2-2x-8\) \(f(x)=x^2-2x-8\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=x^2-2x-8\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_55fe7e4c-ebc6-43b7-96e9-5c03353479ae" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the function from question 2 in vertex form.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=(x-1)^2-9\)</para>
            <para>Complete the square: \(f(x)=x^2 - 2x + 1 - 8 - 1\) \(f(x)=x^2 - 2x + 1 - 8 - 1\) \(f(x)=(x^2 - 2x + 1) - 9\) \(f(x)=(x^2 - 2x + 1) - 9\) \(f(x)=(x-1)^2 - 9\) \(f(x)=(x-1)^2 - 9\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=(x-1)^2-9\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_95479bf9-631e-4a04-ac3e-9a400994015d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Identify the vertex of the quadratic function \(f(x) = (x-1)^2 - 9\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\((1, -9)\)</para>
            <para>\((1, 9)\)</para>
            <para>\((-1, 9)\)</para>
            <para>\((-9, -1)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The vertex is \((1, -9)\).</para>
            <para>The function is written in vertex form: \(f(x) = (x - h)^2 + k\) \(f(x) = (x - h)^2 + k\) \(f(x) = (x - 1)^2 - 9\) \(f(x) = (x - 1)^2 - 9\) \(h = 1\) and \(k = -9\) \(h = 1\) and \(k = -9\) So, the vertex is \((1, -9)\). So, the vertex is \((1, -9)\). </para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \((1, -9)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1ed28060-bc51-4003-91db-cfee70fddd12" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 5 - 6, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at \((-4, 1)\) and also goes through the point \((6, -1)\).</para>
            <para>Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form in simplest form.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( \frac{-1}{50} \)</para>
            <para>\(-1=a(6-(-4))^2+1\) \(-1=a(10)^2+1\) \(-1=a(10)^2+1\) \(-2=100a\) \(-2=100a\) \(a=\frac{-2}{100}=\frac{-1}{50}\) \(a=\frac{-2}{100}=\frac{-1}{50}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \( \frac{-1}{50} \).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5cb3fdfc-ced5-4ef0-ae95-b0c6c6541248" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the equation in vertex form. Hint: Be sure to use y = to denote your equation.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(y=\frac{-1}{50}(x+4)^2+1\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=\frac{-1}{50}(x+4)^2+1\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a801a69a-ce71-4fc4-8cf5-402892a8e844" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 7 and 8, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at \((-2, -3)\) and also goes through the point \((4, 2)\).</para>
            <para>Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form in simplest form.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( \frac{5}{36} \)</para>
            <para>\(2=a(4-(-2))^2+(-3)\) \(2=a(6)^2+(-3)\) \(2=a(6)^2+(-3)\) \(2+3=36a+(-3)+3\) \(2+3=36a+(-3)+3\) \(5=36a\) \(5=36a\) \(a=\frac{5}{36}\) \(a=\frac{5}{36}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(a=\frac{5}{36}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_25dd1a17-d959-45a0-9466-755d9d347cff" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the equation in vertex form. Hint: Be sure to use y = to denote your equation.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(y=\frac{5}{36}(x+2)^2-3\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=\frac{5}{36}(x+2)^2-3\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0ea78142-8d2b-4f7c-ad07-60bf616e0e8c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 9 - 10, use the function \(f(x)=x^2\) that is shifted to create the function \(g(x)\) that has a vertex at \((-4, 6)\).</para>
            <para>Write \(g(x)\) in vertex form.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)</para>
            <para>Substitute the vertex in for \((h, k)\): \(g(x)=(x-(-4))^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x-(-4))^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\).</para>
            <para>Substitute the vertex: \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_60bd9f86-e40b-4662-9244-1f9ad22d5935" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write \(g(x)\) in standard form.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\)</para>
            <para>Expand and simplify: \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)(x+4)+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)(x+4)+6\) \(g(x)=x^2+4x+4x+16+6\) \(g(x)=x^2+4x+4x+16+6\) \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\) \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\).</para>
            <para>Steps: \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)(x+4)+6\) \(g(x)=(x+4)(x+4)+6\) \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\) \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
